    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Traditionalist theologians often argue that modern secular views of marriage, such as same-sex marriage and no-fault divorce, undermine the moral and spiritual values of traditional marriage, citing biblical teachings and natural law principles. They claim that separation of marriage from procreation and redefinition of marriage roles lead to a decline in family integrity, increase in immorality, and a fragmentation of society. Additionally, traditionalists often appeal to the concept of \"natural law,\" arguing that marriage and family are ordained by God, and altering these institutions goes against the divine will. This perspective emphasizes the importance of recognizing the sacred nature of marriage and family in order to preserve the unity and stability of society.",
