      "content": "Traditionalist theologians argue that the erosion of traditional marriage and family norms leads to a profound fragmentation of society, resulting in the breakdown of previously strong family bonds, community ties, and social cohesion. They claim that this erosion undermines the fabric of society by eroding the foundation of morality, identity, and belonging. They warn that the redefinition of marriage goes against the natural human inclinations towards love, commitment, and self-sacrifice, leading to a sense of disorientation and dislocation in individuals, families, and communities. This, in turn, threatens the very foundation of civil society, encouraging individuals to focus on their own interests, rather than cultivating compassion, solidarity, and common good.",
